       "type": "question",
       "label": null,
       "prompt": "$f(x)=x^2-3$.\n\nFor each $g(x)$, simplify $f(g(x))$, hence state the domain.",
       "children": [
        {
         "id": "v2-a6564-p25-practice-j10-084451-j10-q-a",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "a",
         "prompt": "$g(x)=x-2$",
         "answerSpaceMm": 25,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$f(g(x))=x^2-4x+1$, with domain $(-\\infty,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(g(x))&=(x-2)^2-3\\\\&=x^2-4x+1\\end{align*}$$\nSince $g(x)=x-2$ is defined for all $x$, the domain of $f(g(x))$ is all real $x$."
         },
         "questionDiagrams": []
        },
        {
         "id": "v2-a6564-p25-practice-j10-084451-j10-q-b",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "b",
         "prompt": "$g(x)=\\sqrt{x-2}$",
         "answerSpaceMm": 25,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$f(g(x))=x-5$, with domain $[2,\\infty)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(g(x))&=(\\sqrt{x-2})^2-3\\\\&=x-5\\end{align*}$$\nSince the domain of $g(x)$ is $x\\geq2$, the domain of $f(g(x))$ is $x\\geq2$."
         },
         "questionDiagrams": []
        },
        {
         "id": "v2-a6564-p25-practice-j10-084451-j10-q-c",
         "type": "part",
         "label": "c",
         "prompt": "$g(x)=\\dfrac{1}{x-2}$",
         "answerSpaceMm": 25,
         "answer": {
          "short": "$f(g(x))=\\dfrac{1}{(x-2)^2}-3$, with domain $x\\neq2$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}f(g(x))&=\\left(\\dfrac{1}{x-2}\\right)^2-3\\\\&=\\dfrac{1}{(x-2)^2}-3\\end{align*}$$\nSince $g(x)$ is undefined at $x=2$, the domain of $f(g(x))$ is $x\\neq2$."
         },
         "questionDiagrams": []
