       "type": "question",
       "label": null,
       "prompt": "$f(f(x))=x$ for all $x$ in the domain of $f$. The point $(2,5)$ lies on the graph of $y=f(x)$.\n\nWrite down another point on the graph of $y=f(x)$.",
       "answer": {
        "short": "$(5,2)$.",
        "worked": "Since $(2,5)$ lies on the graph, $f(2)=5$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}f(5)&=f(f(2))\\\\f(5)&=2\\end{aligned}$$\nSo $(5,2)$ also lies on the graph. This is the reflection of $(2,5)$ in the line $y=x$."
